%S A118339 1,3,15,63,267,1107,4623,19071,78987,324543,1337511,5483235,22527315,
%T A118339 92200455,377965479,1544925891,6322891707,25817864259,105529742655,
%U A118339 430541924499,1758036418947,7167497991807,29242844975127,119153375775471,485801895166671,1978474220442567,8061781422275019
%N A118339 Number of fixed linear polycubes with n cells.
%C A118339 Gaunt et al. also enumerate clusters with upper limits on the vertex degree.
%C A118339 a(n) is the number of fixed linear or snake polycubes of size n. - _John Mason_, Sep 27 2024
%C A118339 From _Carlo Corti_, Aug 20 2026: (Start)
%C A118339 Previous name was: Number of simple chains with n-1 edges strongly embedded in a simple cubic lattice.
%C A118339 Here "fixed" means that translations are identified, while rotations and reflections are counted as distinct. (End)
%H A118339 Carlo Corti, <a href="/A118339/b118339.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..28</a>
%H A118339 D. S. Gaunt, J. L. Martin, G. Ord, G. M. Torrie, and S. G. Whittington, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1088/0305-4470/13/5/037">Restricted valence site animals on the simple cubic lattice</a>, J. Phys. A: Math. Gen. 13 (1980) 1791-1797.
%H A118339 Y.-H. Hsieh, C.-N. Chen, and C.-K. Hu, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1051/epjconf/201610801005">Exact Partition Functions of Interacting Self-Avoiding Walks on Lattices</a>, EPJ Web Conf. 108 (2016), 01005.
%H A118339 Y.-H. Hsieh, C.-N. Chen, and C.-K. Hu, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cpc.2016.08.006">Efficient algorithm for computing exact partition functions of lattice polymer models</a>, Comput. Phys. Commun. 209 (2016), 27-33.
%F A118339 a(n) = A174319(n-1) / 2 for n > 1. - _Andrei Zabolotskii_, Apr 08 2026
%F A118339 a(n) = 3*Z_n(0) for n >= 2, where Z_N(x) is the N-monomer interacting self-avoiding-walk partition function defined in Eq. (3) of the Hsieh, Chen, and Hu EPJ Web Conf. paper and in Eq. (2) of their Comput. Phys. Commun. paper; the factor 3 restores the three possible lattice axes for the first edge suppressed by their fixed-direction convention. - _Carlo Corti_, Aug 20 2026
%Y A118339 Cf. A182644, A363201, A363202, A174319.
%K A118339 nonn,walk,changed
%O A118339 1,2
%A A118339 _R. J. Mathar_, May 14 2006
%E A118339 a(18)-a(23) using the formula added by _Andrei Zabolotskii_, Apr 08 2026
